IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- s 2(1): the defined terms about PRODUCTS: capital markets products, securities, debentures, derivatives contracts,
-- futures contracts, spot contracts, underlying things, commodities, financial instruments, shares.
-- Imports prelude and daydate only. The units, unitholders and schemes are in sfa-definitions-schemes.l4.
--
-- How to read a function in this module.
--   Every defined term of s 2(1) is ONE function, named `s 2(1) "<term>" <the thing> is <the term>`, over the facts a person could state.
--   The result is MAYBE BOOLEAN:
--     JUST TRUE   the thing is within the term (a limb of the definition is met and no exclusion applies);
--     JUST FALSE  the TEXT says it is not: a definition that says "means" and no limb is met, or an express exclusion ("but does not include");
--     NOTHING     the text does not say: an "includes" definition (an open list) with no listed limb met.
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--   Every branch that answers "no" carries `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "..."`; every branch that
--   answers "not covered" carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`.
--   A limb the Act hands to the Authority, the regulations or another Act ("prescribed", "specified", "as defined in the
--   Banking Act 1970") is an INPUT named for the fact ("the Authority has prescribed ..."), never a thing read from memory.
--   The definitions apply "unless the context otherwise requires" (the chapeau of s 2(1)): that qualification is
--   `s 2(1) the definitions apply unless the context otherwise requires` in sfa-definitions-rest.l4, not repeated here.

§ `s 2(1): capital markets products, securities and the contracts about them`

-- src:1862 | “capital markets products” means any securities, units in a
-- src:1863 | collective investment scheme, derivatives contracts, spot
-- src:1864 | foreign exchange contracts for the purposes of leveraged
-- src:1865 | foreign exchange trading, and such other products as the
-- src:1866 | Authority may prescribe as capital markets products;
@ref s 2(1) "capital markets products" (src:1862-1866)
GIVEN
    `the product is securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the product securities as section 2(1) defines "securities"?
    `the product is a unit in a collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the product a unit in a collective investment scheme?
    `the product is a derivatives contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the product a derivatives contract as section 2(1) defines it?
    `the product is a spot foreign exchange contract for the purposes of leveraged foreign exchange trading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the product a spot foreign exchange contract for the purposes of leveraged foreign exchange trading?
    `the Authority has prescribed the product as capital markets products` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed this product as capital markets products?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "capital markets products" the product is capital markets products` MEANS
    IF `the product is securities` OR `the product is a unit in a collective investment scheme` OR `the product is a derivatives contract` OR `the product is a spot foreign exchange contract for the purposes of leveraged foreign exchange trading` OR `the Authority has prescribed the product as capital markets products`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any securities, units in a collective investment scheme, derivatives contracts, spot foreign exchange contracts for the purposes of leveraged foreign exchange trading, and such other products as the Authority may prescribe"

-- src:3097 | “securities” means —
-- src:3099 | (a) shares, units in a business trust or any instrument
-- src:3100 | conferring or representing a legal or beneficial
-- src:3101 | ownership interest in a corporation, partnership or
-- src:3102 | limited liability partnership;
-- src:3104 | (b) debentures; or
-- src:3106 | (c) any other product or class of products as may be
-- src:3107 | prescribed,
-- src:3112 | but does not include —
-- src:3114 | (d) any unit of a collective investment scheme;
-- src:3116 | (e) any bill of exchange;
-- src:3118 | (f) any certificate of deposit issued by a bank or finance
-- src:3119 | company, whether situated in Singapore or
-- src:3120 | elsewhere; or
-- src:3122 | (g) such other product or class of products as may be
-- src:3123 | prescribed;
@ref s 2(1) "securities" (src:3097-3123)
GIVEN
    `the instrument is a share` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument a share?
    `the instrument is a unit in a business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument a unit in a business trust?
    `the instrument confers or represents a legal or beneficial ownership interest in a corporation, partnership or limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the instrument confer or represent a legal or beneficial ownership interest in a corporation, partnership or limited liability partnership?
    `the instrument is a debenture` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument a debenture as section 2(1) defines "debenture"?
    `the Authority has prescribed the instrument, or its class, as securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed this instrument, or its class of product, as securities?
    `the instrument is a unit of a collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument a unit of a collective investment scheme?
    `the instrument is a bill of exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument a bill of exchange?
    `the instrument is a certificate of deposit issued by a bank or finance company, whether situated in Singapore or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument a certificate of deposit issued by a bank or finance company, in Singapore or elsewhere?
    `the Authority has prescribed the instrument, or its class, as not being securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed this instrument, or its class of product, as not being securities?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "securities" the instrument is securities` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the instrument is a unit of a collective investment scheme` OR `the instrument is a bill of exchange` OR `the instrument is a certificate of deposit issued by a bank or finance company, whether situated in Singapore or elsewhere` OR `the Authority has prescribed the instrument, or its class, as not being securities`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include (d) any unit of a collective investment scheme; (e) any bill of exchange; (f) any certificate of deposit issued by a bank or finance company, whether situated in Singapore or elsewhere; or (g) such other product or class of products as may be prescribed"
        IF `the instrument is a share` OR `the instrument is a unit in a business trust` OR `the instrument confers or represents a legal or beneficial ownership interest in a corporation, partnership or limited liability partnership` OR `the instrument is a debenture` OR `the Authority has prescribed the instrument, or its class, as securities`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means (a) shares, units in a business trust or any instrument conferring or representing a legal or beneficial ownership interest in a corporation, partnership or limited liability partnership; (b) debentures; or (c) any other product or class of products as may be prescribed"

-- src:3125 | “securities‑based derivatives contract” means any derivatives
-- src:3126 | contract of which the underlying thing or any of the
-- src:3127 | underlying things is a security or a securities index, but
-- src:3128 | does not include any derivatives contract that is, or that
-- src:3129 | belongs to a class of derivatives contracts that is, prescribed
-- src:3130 | by regulations made under section 341;
@ref s 2(1) "securities-based derivatives contract" (src:3125-3130)
GIVEN
    `the contract is a derivatives contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract a derivatives contract as section 2(1) defines it?
    `the underlying thing of the contract, or any of its underlying things, is a security or a securities index` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the underlying thing of the contract (or any one of its underlying things) a security or a securities index?
    `regulations under section 341 prescribe the contract, or its class, as not being one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations made under section 341 prescribe this contract, or its class of derivatives contracts?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "securities-based derivatives contract" the contract is a securities-based derivatives contract` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `regulations under section 341 prescribe the contract, or its class, as not being one`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include any derivatives contract that is, or that belongs to a class of derivatives contracts that is, prescribed by regulations made under section 341"
        IF `the contract is a derivatives contract` AND `the underlying thing of the contract, or any of its underlying things, is a security or a securities index`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any derivatives contract of which the underlying thing or any of the underlying things is a security or a securities index"

-- src:3138 | “specified products” means securities, specified securities‑based
-- src:3139 | derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment
-- src:3140 | scheme;
@ref s 2(1) "specified products" (src:3138-3140)
GIVEN
    `the product is securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the product securities as section 2(1) defines "securities"?
    `the product is a specified securities-based derivatives contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the product a specified securities-based derivatives contract (a securities-based derivatives contract that is not a futures contract)?
    `the product is a unit in a collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the product a unit in a collective investment scheme?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "specified products" the product is a specified product` MEANS
    IF `the product is securities` OR `the product is a specified securities-based derivatives contract` OR `the product is a unit in a collective investment scheme`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means securities, specified securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme"

-- src:3142 | “specified securities‑based derivatives contract” means a
-- src:3143 | securities‑based derivatives contract that is not a futures
-- src:3144 | contract;
@ref s 2(1) "specified securities-based derivatives contract" (src:3142-3144)
GIVEN
    `the contract is a securities-based derivatives contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract a securities-based derivatives contract as section 2(1) defines it?
    `the contract is a futures contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract a futures contract as section 2(1) defines it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "specified securities-based derivatives contract" the contract is a specified securities-based derivatives contract` MEANS
    IF `the contract is a securities-based derivatives contract` AND (NOT `the contract is a futures contract`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a securities-based derivatives contract that is not a futures contract"

-- src:3146 | “spot contract” means a contract or an arrangement for the sale
-- src:3147 | or purchase of any underlying thing at the spot price, where it
-- src:3148 | is intended for a party to the contract or arrangement to take
-- src:3149 | delivery of the underlying thing immediately or within a
-- src:3150 | period which must not be longer than the period determined
-- src:3151 | by the market convention for delivery of the underlying
-- src:3152 | thing;
@ref s 2(1) "spot contract" (src:3146-3152)
GIVEN
    `the contract or arrangement is for the sale or purchase of an underlying thing at the spot price` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract or arrangement for the sale or purchase of an underlying thing at the spot price?
    `it is intended for a party to take delivery of the underlying thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a party intended to take delivery of the underlying thing?
    `the number of days within which delivery is intended to be taken (0 if immediately)` IS A NUMBER @desc Within how many days is delivery intended to be taken (0 if immediately)?
    `the number of days the market convention allows for delivery of the underlying thing` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days does the market convention allow for delivery of this underlying thing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "spot contract" the contract or arrangement is a spot contract` MEANS
    IF `the contract or arrangement is for the sale or purchase of an underlying thing at the spot price` AND `it is intended for a party to take delivery of the underlying thing` AND `the number of days within which delivery is intended to be taken (0 if immediately)` AT MOST `the number of days the market convention allows for delivery of the underlying thing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a contract or an arrangement for the sale or purchase of any underlying thing at the spot price, where it is intended for a party to the contract or arrangement to take delivery of the underlying thing immediately or within a period which must not be longer than the period determined by the market convention for delivery of the underlying thing"

-- src:3154 | “spot foreign exchange contract” has the meaning given in the
-- src:3155 | Second Schedule;
@ref s 2(1) "spot foreign exchange contract" (src:3154-3155)
GIVEN
    `the contract meets the Second Schedule meaning of a spot foreign exchange contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the contract meet the meaning of "spot foreign exchange contract" that the Second Schedule gives?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "spot foreign exchange contract" the contract is a spot foreign exchange contract` MEANS
    IF `the contract meets the Second Schedule meaning of a spot foreign exchange contract`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has the meaning given in the Second Schedule"

-- src:3337 | “underlying thing” means —
-- src:3339 | (a) in relation to a derivatives contract or a spot
-- src:3340 | contract —
-- src:3342 | (i) a unit in a collective investment scheme;
-- src:3347 | (ii) a commodity;
-- src:3349 | (iii) a financial instrument;
-- src:3351 | (iv) the credit of any person; or
-- src:3353 | (v) an arrangement, event, index, intangible
-- src:3354 | property, tangible property or transaction that
-- src:3355 | is, or that belongs to a class of arrangements,
-- src:3356 | events, indices, intangible properties, tangible
-- src:3357 | properties or transactions that is, prescribed by
-- src:3358 | regulations made under section 341 to be an
-- src:3359 | underlying thing in relation to a derivatives
-- src:3360 | contract or a spot contract,
-- src:3362 | (a) but does not include any arrangement, event, index,
-- src:3363 | intangible property, tangible property or transaction
-- src:3364 | that is, or that belongs to a class of arrangements,
-- src:3365 | events, indices, intangible properties, tangible
-- src:3366 | properties or transactions that is, prescribed by
-- src:3367 | regulations made under section 341 not to be an
-- src:3368 | underlying thing in relation to a derivatives contract
-- src:3369 | or a spot contract; and
-- src:3371 | (b) in relation to a financial benchmark —
-- src:3373 | (i) an investment product as defined in
-- src:3374 | section 2(1) of the Financial Advisers
-- src:3375 | Act 2001;
-- src:3377 | (ii) a commodity;
-- src:3379 | (iii) a financial instrument;
-- src:3381 | (iv) any intangible property or class of intangible
-- src:3382 | properties; or
-- src:3384 | (v) any arrangement, event or transaction that is, or
-- src:3385 | that belongs to a class of arrangements, events
-- src:3386 | or transactions that is, prescribed by regulations
-- src:3387 | made under section 341 to be an underlying
-- src:3388 | thing in relation to a financial benchmark,
-- src:3390 | (b) but does not include any arrangement, event,
-- src:3391 | intangible property or transaction that is, or that
-- src:3396 | belongs to a class of arrangements, events, intangible
-- src:3397 | properties or transactions that is, prescribed by
-- src:3398 | regulations made under section 341 not to be an
-- src:3399 | underlying thing in relation to a financial benchmark;
@ref s 2(1) "underlying thing" (src:3337-3399)
GIVEN
    `the thing is a unit in a collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a unit in a collective investment scheme?
    `the thing is a commodity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a commodity as section 2(1) defines "commodity"?
    `the thing is a financial instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a financial instrument as section 2(1) defines it?
    `the thing is the credit of a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing the credit of any person?
    `regulations under section 341 prescribe the thing, or its class, to be an underlying thing in relation to a derivatives contract or a spot contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations made under section 341 prescribe this arrangement, event, index, property or transaction (or its class) to be an underlying thing for a derivatives contract or a spot contract?
    `regulations under section 341 prescribe the thing, or its class, not to be an underlying thing in relation to a derivatives contract or a spot contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations made under section 341 prescribe this arrangement, event, index, property or transaction (or its class) not to be an underlying thing for a derivatives contract or a spot contract?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "underlying thing" (a) the thing is an underlying thing in relation to a derivatives contract or a spot contract` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `regulations under section 341 prescribe the thing, or its class, not to be an underlying thing in relation to a derivatives contract or a spot contract`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include any arrangement, event, index, intangible property, tangible property or transaction that is, or that belongs to a class ... prescribed by regulations made under section 341 not to be an underlying thing in relation to a derivatives contract or a spot contract"
        IF `the thing is a unit in a collective investment scheme` OR `the thing is a commodity` OR `the thing is a financial instrument` OR `the thing is the credit of a person` OR `regulations under section 341 prescribe the thing, or its class, to be an underlying thing in relation to a derivatives contract or a spot contract`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means ... (a) in relation to a derivatives contract or a spot contract ..."

@ref s 2(1) "underlying thing" (b) (src:3371-3399)
GIVEN
    `the thing is an investment product as defined in section 2(1) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing an investment product as section 2(1) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001 defines it?
    `the thing is a commodity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a commodity as section 2(1) defines "commodity"?
    `the thing is a financial instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a financial instrument as section 2(1) defines it?
    `the thing is intangible property or a class of intangible properties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing intangible property, or a class of intangible properties?
    `regulations under section 341 prescribe the thing, or its class, to be an underlying thing in relation to a financial benchmark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations made under section 341 prescribe this arrangement, event or transaction (or its class) to be an underlying thing for a financial benchmark?
    `regulations under section 341 prescribe the thing, or its class, not to be an underlying thing in relation to a financial benchmark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations made under section 341 prescribe this arrangement, event, intangible property or transaction (or its class) not to be an underlying thing for a financial benchmark?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "underlying thing" (b) the thing is an underlying thing in relation to a financial benchmark` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `regulations under section 341 prescribe the thing, or its class, not to be an underlying thing in relation to a financial benchmark`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include any arrangement, event, intangible property or transaction that is, or that belongs to a class ... prescribed by regulations made under section 341 not to be an underlying thing in relation to a financial benchmark"
        IF `the thing is an investment product as defined in section 2(1) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001` OR `the thing is a commodity` OR `the thing is a financial instrument` OR `the thing is intangible property or a class of intangible properties` OR `regulations under section 341 prescribe the thing, or its class, to be an underlying thing in relation to a financial benchmark`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means ... (b) in relation to a financial benchmark ..."

-- src:2194 | “commodity” means —
-- src:2196 | (a) any produce, item, goods or article;
-- src:2198 | (b) any index, right or interest in any produce, item,
-- src:2199 | goods or article; or
-- src:2201 | (c) any index, right, interest, tangible property or
-- src:2202 | intangible property of any nature that is, or belongs
-- src:2207 | to a class of indices, rights, interests, tangible
-- src:2208 | properties or intangible properties that is,
-- src:2209 | prescribed for the purposes of this definition,
-- src:2211 | but does not include —
-- src:2213 | (d) any produce, item, goods or article that is, or that
-- src:2214 | belongs to a class of produce, items, goods or articles
-- src:2215 | that is, prescribed not to be a commodity for the
-- src:2216 | purposes of this definition; or
-- src:2218 | (e) any index, right or interest in any produce, item,
-- src:2219 | goods or article that is, or that belongs to a class of
-- src:2220 | indices, rights or interests that is, prescribed not to be
-- src:2221 | a commodity for the purposes of this definition;
@ref s 2(1) "commodity" (src:2194-2221)
GIVEN
    `the thing is a produce, item, goods or article` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a produce, item, goods or article?
    `the thing is an index, right or interest in a produce, item, goods or article` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing an index, right or interest in a produce, item, goods or article?
    `the thing is an index, right, interest, tangible property or intangible property that is, or belongs to a class that is, prescribed as a commodity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing an index, right, interest, tangible property or intangible property that is prescribed (alone or as a class) as a commodity?
    `the thing is a produce, item, goods or article that is, or belongs to a class that is, prescribed not to be a commodity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a produce, item, goods or article that is prescribed (alone or as a class) not to be a commodity?
    `the thing is an index, right or interest in a produce, item, goods or article that is, or belongs to a class that is, prescribed not to be a commodity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing an index, right or interest in a produce, item, goods or article that is prescribed (alone or as a class) not to be a commodity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "commodity" the thing is a commodity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the thing is a produce, item, goods or article that is, or belongs to a class that is, prescribed not to be a commodity` OR `the thing is an index, right or interest in a produce, item, goods or article that is, or belongs to a class that is, prescribed not to be a commodity`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include (d) any produce, item, goods or article that is ... prescribed not to be a commodity ...; or (e) any index, right or interest in any produce, item, goods or article that is ... prescribed not to be a commodity"
        IF `the thing is a produce, item, goods or article` OR `the thing is an index, right or interest in a produce, item, goods or article` OR `the thing is an index, right, interest, tangible property or intangible property that is, or belongs to a class that is, prescribed as a commodity`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means (a) any produce, item, goods or article; (b) any index, right or interest in any produce, item, goods or article; or (c) any index, right, interest, tangible property or intangible property of any nature that is, or belongs ... prescribed for the purposes of this definition"

-- src:2545 | “financial instrument” includes any currency, currency index,
-- src:2546 | interest rate, interest rate instrument, interest rate index,
-- src:2547 | securities, securities index, a group or groups of such
-- src:2548 | financial instruments, and any other thing that is prescribed
-- src:2549 | by the Authority by regulations made under section 341 for
-- src:2550 | the purposes of this definition;
@ref s 2(1) "financial instrument" (src:2545-2550)
GIVEN
    `the thing is a currency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a currency?
    `the thing is a currency index` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a currency index?
    `the thing is an interest rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing an interest rate?
    `the thing is an interest rate instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing an interest rate instrument?
    `the thing is an interest rate index` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing an interest rate index?
    `the thing is securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing securities as section 2(1) defines "securities"?
    `the thing is a securities index` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a securities index?
    `the thing is a group or groups of such financial instruments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a group, or groups, of financial instruments of the kinds just listed?
    `the Authority has prescribed the thing by regulations under section 341 as a financial instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed this thing, by regulations under section 341, for the purposes of the definition of "financial instrument"?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "financial instrument" the thing is a financial instrument` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a currency` OR `the thing is a currency index` OR `the thing is an interest rate` OR `the thing is an interest rate instrument` OR `the thing is an interest rate index` OR `the thing is securities` OR `the thing is a securities index` OR `the thing is a group or groups of such financial instruments` OR `the Authority has prescribed the thing by regulations under section 341 as a financial instrument`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes any currency, currency index, interest rate, ... and any other thing that is prescribed" lists without closing the list

-- src:2354 | “derivatives contract” means —
-- src:2356 | (a) any contract or arrangement under which —
-- src:2358 | (i) a party to the contract or arrangement is
-- src:2359 | required to, or may be required to, discharge
-- src:2360 | all or any of its obligations under the contract or
-- src:2361 | arrangement at some future time; and
-- src:2363 | (ii) the value of the contract or arrangement is
-- src:2364 | determined (whether directly or indirectly, or
-- src:2365 | whether wholly or in part) by reference to, is
-- src:2366 | derived from, or varies by reference to, either
-- src:2367 | of the following:
-- src:2369 | (A) the value or amount of one or more
-- src:2370 | underlying things;
-- src:2372 | (B) fluctuations in the values or amounts of
-- src:2373 | one or more underlying things; or
-- src:2375 | (b) any contract or arrangement that is, or that belongs to
-- src:2376 | a class of contracts or arrangements that is,
-- src:2377 | prescribed to be a derivatives contract,
-- src:2379 | but does not include —
-- src:2381 | (c) securities;
-- src:2383 | (d) any unit in a collective investment scheme;
-- src:2385 | (e) a spot contract;
-- src:2387 | (f) a deposit as defined in section 4B of the Banking
-- src:2388 | Act 1970, where the deposit is accepted by a bank or
-- src:2389 | merchant bank licensed under that Act;
-- src:2391 | (g) a deposit as defined in section 2 of the Finance
-- src:2392 | Companies Act 1967, where the deposit is accepted
-- src:2397 | by a finance company as defined in that section of
-- src:2398 | that Act;
-- src:2400 | (h) any contract of insurance in relation to any class of
-- src:2401 | insurance business specified in section 3(1) of the
-- src:2402 | Insurance Act 1966; or
-- src:2404 | (i) any contract or arrangement that is, or that belongs to
-- src:2405 | a class of contracts or arrangements that is,
-- src:2406 | prescribed not to be a derivatives contract;
@ref s 2(1) "derivatives contract" (src:2354-2406)
GIVEN
    `a party is required, or may be required, to discharge all or any of its obligations at some future time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a party to the contract or arrangement required, or liable to be required, to discharge any of its obligations at some future time?
    `its value is determined, directly or indirectly, wholly or in part, by reference to the value of one or more underlying things or to fluctuations in their values` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the value of the contract or arrangement determined (directly or indirectly, wholly or in part) by reference to, derived from, or varies with, the value or amount of one or more underlying things, or fluctuations in them?
    `the contract or arrangement is, or belongs to a class that is, prescribed to be a derivatives contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract or arrangement (or its class) prescribed to be a derivatives contract?
    `the contract or arrangement is securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract or arrangement securities as section 2(1) defines "securities"?
    `the contract or arrangement is a unit in a collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract or arrangement a unit in a collective investment scheme?
    `the contract or arrangement is a spot contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract or arrangement a spot contract as section 2(1) defines it?
    `the contract or arrangement is a deposit as defined in section 4B of the Banking Act 1970 accepted by a bank or merchant bank licensed under that Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract or arrangement a deposit (section 4B of the Banking Act 1970) accepted by a bank or merchant bank licensed under that Act?
    `the contract or arrangement is a deposit as defined in section 2 of the Finance Companies Act 1967 accepted by a finance company as defined in that section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract or arrangement a deposit (section 2 of the Finance Companies Act 1967) accepted by a finance company as defined there?
    `the contract or arrangement is a contract of insurance in relation to a class of insurance business specified in section 3(1) of the Insurance Act 1966` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract or arrangement a contract of insurance in a class of insurance business specified in section 3(1) of the Insurance Act 1966?
    `the contract or arrangement is, or belongs to a class that is, prescribed not to be a derivatives contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract or arrangement (or its class) prescribed not to be a derivatives contract?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "derivatives contract" the contract or arrangement is a derivatives contract` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the contract or arrangement is securities` OR `the contract or arrangement is a unit in a collective investment scheme` OR `the contract or arrangement is a spot contract` OR `the contract or arrangement is a deposit as defined in section 4B of the Banking Act 1970 accepted by a bank or merchant bank licensed under that Act` OR `the contract or arrangement is a deposit as defined in section 2 of the Finance Companies Act 1967 accepted by a finance company as defined in that section` OR `the contract or arrangement is a contract of insurance in relation to a class of insurance business specified in section 3(1) of the Insurance Act 1966` OR `the contract or arrangement is, or belongs to a class that is, prescribed not to be a derivatives contract`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include (c) securities; (d) any unit in a collective investment scheme; (e) a spot contract; (f) a deposit ... accepted by a bank or merchant bank ...; (g) a deposit ... accepted by a finance company ...; (h) any contract of insurance ...; or (i) any contract or arrangement that is ... prescribed not to be a derivatives contract"
        IF (`a party is required, or may be required, to discharge all or any of its obligations at some future time` AND `its value is determined, directly or indirectly, wholly or in part, by reference to the value of one or more underlying things or to fluctuations in their values`) OR `the contract or arrangement is, or belongs to a class that is, prescribed to be a derivatives contract`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means (a) any contract or arrangement under which (i) a party ... is required to, or may be required to, discharge all or any of its obligations ... at some future time; and (ii) the value ... is determined ... by reference to ... underlying things; or (b) any contract or arrangement that is ... prescribed to be a derivatives contract"

-- src:2423 | “exchange‑traded derivatives contract” means a derivatives
-- src:2424 | contract —
-- src:2426 | (a) that is executed on an organised market and is or will
-- src:2427 | be cleared or settled by a clearing facility under an
-- src:2428 | arrangement, process, mechanism or service by
-- src:2429 | which the parties to the derivatives contract
-- src:2430 | substitute or will substitute, through novation or
-- src:2431 | otherwise, the credit of the clearing facility for the
-- src:2432 | credit of the parties to the derivatives contract; and
-- src:2434 | (b) the contractual terms (other than price) of which —
-- src:2436 | (i) are in the same form as the contractual terms of
-- src:2437 | other derivatives contracts of the same type that
-- src:2438 | are executed on the organised market on which
-- src:2439 | the derivatives contract is executed; and
-- src:2444 | (ii) conform to a standard that is provided under the
-- src:2445 | business rules or practices of the organised
-- src:2446 | market on which the derivatives contract is
-- src:2447 | executed,
-- src:2449 | but does not include —
-- src:2451 | (c) any contract under which every contractual term can
-- src:2452 | be negotiated; or
-- src:2454 | (d) any derivatives contract that is, or that belongs to a
-- src:2455 | class of derivatives contracts that is, prescribed not to
-- src:2456 | be an exchange‑traded derivatives contract;
@ref s 2(1) "exchange-traded derivatives contract" (src:2423-2456)
GIVEN
    `the contract is a derivatives contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract a derivatives contract as section 2(1) defines it?
    `the contract is executed on an organised market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract executed on an organised market?
    `the contract is or will be cleared or settled by a clearing facility under an arrangement by which the parties substitute the credit of the clearing facility for their own` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract (or will it be) cleared or settled by a clearing facility under an arrangement by which the parties substitute, through novation or otherwise, the clearing facility's credit for their own?
    `its contractual terms other than price are in the same form as those of other derivatives contracts of the same type on that organised market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are its contractual terms (other than price) in the same form as those of other derivatives contracts of the same type executed on that organised market?
    `its contractual terms other than price conform to a standard provided under the business rules or practices of that organised market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do its contractual terms (other than price) conform to a standard provided under the business rules or practices of that organised market?
    `every contractual term of the contract can be negotiated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can every contractual term of the contract be negotiated?
    `the contract, or its class, is prescribed not to be an exchange-traded derivatives contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract (or its class of derivatives contracts) prescribed not to be an exchange-traded derivatives contract?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "exchange-traded derivatives contract" the derivatives contract is an exchange-traded derivatives contract` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `every contractual term of the contract can be negotiated` OR `the contract, or its class, is prescribed not to be an exchange-traded derivatives contract`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include (c) any contract under which every contractual term can be negotiated; or (d) any derivatives contract that is, or that belongs to a class of derivatives contracts that is, prescribed not to be an exchange-traded derivatives contract"
        IF `the contract is a derivatives contract` AND `the contract is executed on an organised market` AND `the contract is or will be cleared or settled by a clearing facility under an arrangement by which the parties substitute the credit of the clearing facility for their own` AND `its contractual terms other than price are in the same form as those of other derivatives contracts of the same type on that organised market` AND `its contractual terms other than price conform to a standard provided under the business rules or practices of that organised market`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a derivatives contract (a) that is executed on an organised market and is or will be cleared or settled by a clearing facility ...; and (b) the contractual terms (other than price) of which (i) are in the same form ...; and (ii) conform to a standard ..."

-- src:2611 | “futures contract” means —
-- src:2613 | (a) an exchange‑traded derivatives contract under
-- src:2614 | which —
-- src:2616 | (i) one party agrees to transfer title to an
-- src:2617 | underlying thing, or a specified quantity of an
-- src:2618 | underlying thing, to another party at a specified
-- src:2619 | future time and at a specified price payable at
-- src:2620 | that future time; or
-- src:2622 | (ii) the parties will discharge their obligations
-- src:2623 | under the contract by settling the difference
-- src:2624 | between the value of a specified quantity of an
-- src:2625 | underlying thing agreed at the time of the
-- src:2630 | making of the contract and at a specified future
-- src:2631 | time; or
-- src:2633 | (b) an exchange‑traded derivatives contract which is an
-- src:2634 | option on an exchange‑traded derivatives contract
-- src:2635 | mentioned in paragraph (a);
@ref s 2(1) "futures contract" (src:2611-2635)
GIVEN
    `the contract is an exchange-traded derivatives contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract an exchange-traded derivatives contract as section 2(1) defines it?
    `under the contract one party agrees to transfer title to an underlying thing, or a specified quantity of one, to another at a specified future time at a specified price payable at that time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under the contract, does one party agree to transfer title to an underlying thing (or a specified quantity of one) to another at a specified future time and at a specified price payable then?
    `the parties will discharge their obligations under the contract by settling the difference between the value of a specified quantity of an underlying thing at the time of the contract and at a specified future time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will the parties discharge their obligations by settling the difference between the value of a specified quantity of an underlying thing agreed when the contract was made and its value at a specified future time?
    `the contract is an option on an exchange-traded derivatives contract of the kind described in the first two limbs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract an option on an exchange-traded derivatives contract under which title is transferred, or a difference settled, as just described?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "futures contract" the contract is a futures contract` MEANS
    IF `the contract is an exchange-traded derivatives contract` AND (`under the contract one party agrees to transfer title to an underlying thing, or a specified quantity of one, to another at a specified future time at a specified price payable at that time` OR `the parties will discharge their obligations under the contract by settling the difference between the value of a specified quantity of an underlying thing at the time of the contract and at a specified future time` OR `the contract is an option on an exchange-traded derivatives contract of the kind described in the first two limbs`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means (a) an exchange-traded derivatives contract under which (i) one party agrees to transfer title ...; or (ii) the parties will discharge their obligations ... by settling the difference ...; or (b) an exchange-traded derivatives contract which is an option on an exchange-traded derivatives contract mentioned in paragraph (a)"

-- src:2312 | “debenture” includes —
-- src:2314 | (a) any debenture stock, bond, note and any other debt
-- src:2315 | securities issued by or proposed to be issued by a
-- src:2316 | corporation or any other entity, whether constituting a
-- src:2317 | charge or not, on the assets of the issuer;
-- src:2319 | (b) any debenture stock, bond, note and any other debt
-- src:2320 | securities issued by or proposed to be issued by a
-- src:2321 | trustee‑manager of a business trust in its capacity as
-- src:2322 | trustee‑manager of the business trust, or a trustee of a
-- src:2323 | real estate investment trust in its capacity as trustee of
-- src:2324 | the real estate investment trust, whether constituting
-- src:2325 | a charge or not, on the assets of the business trust or
-- src:2326 | real estate investment trust; or
-- src:2328 | (c) such other product or class of products as the
-- src:2329 | Authority may prescribe,
-- src:2331 | but does not include —
-- src:2333 | (d) a cheque, letter of credit, order for the payment of
-- src:2334 | money or bill of exchange; or
-- src:2336 | (e) for the purposes of the application of this definition to
-- src:2337 | a provision of this Act in respect of which any
-- src:2338 | regulations made under that provision provide that
-- src:2339 | the word “debenture” does not include a prescribed
-- src:2340 | document or a document included in a prescribed
-- src:2341 | class of documents, that document or a document
-- src:2342 | included in that class of documents, as the case may
-- src:2343 | be;
@ref s 2(1) "debenture" (src:2312-2343)
GIVEN
    `the instrument is a debenture stock, bond, note or other debt security issued, or proposed to be issued, by a corporation or any other entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument a debenture stock, bond, note or other debt security issued, or proposed to be issued, by a corporation or any other entity (whether or not it is a charge on the issuer's assets)?
    `the instrument is a debenture stock, bond, note or other debt security issued, or proposed to be issued, by a trustee-manager of a business trust or a trustee of a real estate investment trust in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument a debenture stock, bond, note or other debt security issued, or proposed to be issued, by a trustee-manager of a business trust, or by a trustee of a real estate investment trust, in that capacity?
    `the Authority has prescribed the product, or its class, as a debenture` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed this product, or its class of products, as a debenture?
    `the instrument is a cheque, letter of credit, order for the payment of money or bill of exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument a cheque, letter of credit, order for the payment of money or bill of exchange?
    `regulations under the provision in question say that the word debenture does not include the document or its class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the provision you are asking about, do its regulations say that "debenture" does not include this document (or its class of documents)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "debenture" the instrument is a debenture` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the instrument is a cheque, letter of credit, order for the payment of money or bill of exchange` OR `regulations under the provision in question say that the word debenture does not include the document or its class`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include (d) a cheque, letter of credit, order for the payment of money or bill of exchange; or (e) ... that document or a document included in that class of documents"
        IF `the instrument is a debenture stock, bond, note or other debt security issued, or proposed to be issued, by a corporation or any other entity` OR `the instrument is a debenture stock, bond, note or other debt security issued, or proposed to be issued, by a trustee-manager of a business trust or a trustee of a real estate investment trust in that capacity` OR `the Authority has prescribed the product, or its class, as a debenture`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "debenture includes (a) ... (b) ... (c) such other product or class of products as the Authority may prescribe" lists without closing the list

-- src:3135 | “share” has the meaning given by section 4(1) of the Companies
-- src:3136 | Act 1967;
@ref s 2(1) "share" (src:3135-3136)
GIVEN
    `the interest is a share within section 4(1) of the Companies Act 1967` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the interest a share as section 4(1) of the Companies Act 1967 defines the word?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "share" the interest is a share` MEANS
    IF `the interest is a share within section 4(1) of the Companies Act 1967`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has the meaning given by section 4(1) of the Companies Act 1967"

-- src:3460 | “voting share” has the meaning given by section 4(1) of the
-- src:3461 | Companies Act 1967;
@ref s 2(1) "voting share" (src:3460-3461)
GIVEN
    `the share is a voting share within section 4(1) of the Companies Act 1967` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the share a voting share as section 4(1) of the Companies Act 1967 defines the term?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "voting share" the share is a voting share` MEANS
    IF `the share is a voting share within section 4(1) of the Companies Act 1967`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has the meaning given by section 4(1) of the Companies Act 1967"

-- src:2351 | “derivative”, in relation to a unit in a business trust, has the
-- src:2352 | meaning given by section 2 of the Business Trusts Act 2004;
@ref s 2(1) "derivative" (src:2351-2352)
GIVEN
    `the thing is a derivative of a unit in a business trust within section 2 of the Business Trusts Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a derivative of a unit in a business trust, as section 2 of the Business Trusts Act 2004 defines "derivative"?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "derivative" the thing is a derivative of a unit in a business trust` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a derivative of a unit in a business trust within section 2 of the Business Trusts Act 2004`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has the meaning given by section 2 of the Business Trusts Act 2004"

-- src:3305 | “treasury share” —
-- src:3307 | (a) in relation to a company, has the meaning given by
-- src:3308 | section 4(1) of the Companies Act 1967; and
-- src:3310 | (b) in relation to a corporation (other than a company),
-- src:3311 | means any share equivalent to a treasury share in a
-- src:3312 | company;
@ref s 2(1) "treasury share" (src:3305-3312)
GIVEN
    `the share is a treasury share within section 4(1) of the Companies Act 1967` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the share a treasury share as section 4(1) of the Companies Act 1967 defines the term?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "treasury share" (a) the share of a company is a treasury share` MEANS
    IF `the share is a treasury share within section 4(1) of the Companies Act 1967`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to a company, has the meaning given by section 4(1) of the Companies Act 1967"

GIVEN
    `the share is equivalent to a treasury share in a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the share (of a corporation that is not a company) equivalent to a treasury share in a company?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "treasury share" (b) the share of a corporation other than a company is a treasury share` MEANS
    IF `the share is equivalent to a treasury share in a company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to a corporation (other than a company), means any share equivalent to a treasury share in a company"
